msgid "Page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Go to page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Display Builder to enable live search, city and group filters, and sorting. On tables, visitors can click sortable column headers to switch between ascending and descending order. The result count, reset control, and pagination update immediately. In map and map-table layouts, filtering and searching also update the visible markers, and selecting a marker highlights the matching branch in the table. On small screens, tables switch to a compact card-like presentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "12 results"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use two fingers to move the map"
msgstr ""

msgid "Show sort control"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Display Builder to enable live search, city and group filters, and sorting. You can also choose whether to show the visitor sorting control; in table layouts, visitors can still click sortable column headers when sorting is enabled. The result count, reset control, and pagination update immediately. In map and map-table layouts, filtering and searching also update the visible markers, and selecting a marker highlights the matching branch in the table. On small screens, tables switch to a compact card-like presentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Table and map stay connected"
msgstr ""

msgid "In Map + Table, clicking a branch row centers the map on that branch and opens its marker. Clicking a map marker selects and highlights the matching row; when pagination is enabled, the table moves to the page containing that branch. Search and filters update the visible markers at the same time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Filter or search"
msgstr ""

msgid "Select a row or marker"
msgstr ""

msgid "Inspect the location"
msgstr ""

msgid "Table is best for comparing many fields at once. Cards give each branch a more spacious visual block. List is a compact horizontal directory for larger branch sets. Accordion saves space by revealing details on demand. Map focuses on geography, while Map + Table combines the map with the data table."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mobile map controls"
msgstr ""

msgid "On desktop, drag the map with the mouse. On touch screens, one finger is reserved for normal page scrolling; use two fingers to move the map. Zoom controls remain available on the map."
msgstr ""

msgid "Performance"
msgstr ""

msgid "For large branch directories, use pagination and only enable the fields, filters, and map features you need. Map layouts use valid coordinates only, while search, sorting, and filtering run on the loaded branch data without a page reload."
msgstr ""

msgid "How does the table search work?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Click the search icon in the table header to open the search field. Search matches branch name, city, address, phone, and group. The field stays focused while you type and can be cleared with the × button."
msgstr ""

msgid "How do I sort a table?"
msgstr ""

msgid "When sorting is enabled, click the Branch, City, or Group column heading. The arrow shows the active direction. There is no separate sorting control in the visitor interface."
msgstr ""

msgid "Select multiple branches or groups from their tables. You can delete the selected items at once, or open Display Builder to generate one shortcode that combines all selected items."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Display Builder to enable live search, city and group filters, and sorting. In table layouts, visitors sort directly by clicking sortable column headers; there is no separate sorting box. The search button opens the search field without leaving the table header. Result counts, reset, and pagination update immediately without reloading the page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Map interaction"
msgstr ""

msgid "For XLSX or CSV, use columns such as Name, City, Address, Phone, Lat, Lng, and Group. The downloadable XLSX template contains column instructions and no sample locations. Preview the import before running it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cannot parse worksheet data."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cannot read shared strings."
msgstr ""

msgid "Developed by"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kashida Branch Locator stores branch, address, phone, coordinate, and group information entered by site administrators in the WordPress database. The plugin does not send this data to Kashida servers. When map layouts are used, visitors' browsers request map tiles from OpenStreetMap. When a visitor chooses Directions, the browser opens Google Maps. Site owners should review the privacy policies of those services for their own sites."
msgstr ""

